1
00:03:46,363 --> 00:03:52,363
Odd ducks welcome.

2
00:07:32,727 --> 00:07:38,727
Migration is a family, comedy, adventure film directed by Benjamin Renner.

3
00:11:19,090 --> 00:11:25,090
After a migrating duck family alights on their pond with thrilling tales of far-flung places, the Mallard
family embarks on a family road trip, from New England, to New York City, to tropical Jamaica.

4
00:15:05,454 --> 00:15:11,454
Mack Mallard (voice), played by Kumail Nanjiani.

5
00:18:51,818 --> 00:18:57,818
Pam Mallard (voice), played by Elizabeth Banks.

6
00:22:38,181 --> 00:22:44,181
Dax Mallard (voice), played by Caspar Jennings.

7
00:26:24,545 --> 00:26:30,545
Gwen Mallard (voice), played by Tresi Gazal.

8
00:30:10,909 --> 00:30:16,909
Chump (voice), played by Awkwafina.

9
00:33:57,272 --> 00:34:03,272
Erin (voice), played by Carol Kane.

10
00:37:43,636 --> 00:37:49,636
Migration is a 2023 American animated adventure comedy film
directed by Benjamin Renner and written by Mike White.

11
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:36,000
Produced by Illumination and distributed by Universal Pictures, the film stars the voices of
Kumail Nanjiani, Elizabeth Banks, Keegan-Michael Key, Awkwafina, and Danny DeVito.

12
00:45:16,363 --> 00:45:22,363
The story follows a family of mallards who try to convince their overprotective father to go on a vacation
of a lifetime and attempt to migrate from New England, through New York City, to Jamaica.

13
00:49:02,727 --> 00:49:08,727
Illumination announced Migration in February 2022, with Renner and
White attached as director and writer, respectively.

14
00:52:49,090 --> 00:52:55,090
Renner, who had previously helmed traditionally animated films, including
Ernest & Celestine (2012) and The Big Bad Fox and Other Tales...

15
00:56:35,454 --> 00:56:41,454
(2017), was tasked with adapting his simple drawing
style for a computer-animated film.

16
01:00:21,818 --> 01:00:27,818
In hiring Renner, studio head and producer Chris Meledandri sought to focus on a
filmmaker's vision for the project in comparison with Illumination's recent films.

17
01:04:08,181 --> 01:04:14,181
John Powell composed the score, marking his second collaboration
with Illumination following The Lorax (2012).

18
01:07:54,545 --> 01:08:00,545
Migration premiered at the VIEW Conference in Turin, Italy, on October 19, 2023,
and was theatrically released in the United States on December 22.

19
01:11:40,909 --> 01:11:46,909
The film received mixed reviews from critics and
grossed $300.5 million worldwide.

20
01:15:27,272 --> 01:15:33,272
The film explores themes of duck, villain, migration, flight, anthropomorphism.

21
01:19:13,636 --> 01:19:19,636
The tone is lighthearted and intense.
